# Line endings. LF in the repo for everything text, because the tree is
# authored on Linux and macOS -- except the Windows scripts, which get CRLF on
# checkout. A .bat file with LF-only endings misparses `goto` across
# parenthesised blocks, which is a failure that reads as a logic bug rather
# than a line-ending one.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Vendored JavaScript. linguist-vendored keeps GitHub from reporting this as a
# JavaScript project: cytoscape.min.js alone outweighs every .go file in the
# tree, and the language bar is the first thing a visitor reads. -diff stops
# git from trying to diff a minified bundle.
internal/mapweb/assets/vendor/** linguist-vendored
*.min.js -diff

# Licence texts are not written here and should not count as source.
licenses/** linguist-vendored
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md linguist-generated

# Binary, so git never rewrites them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
